## Practice task (component type: NORMALIZER)

I am building a North American sports and entertainment customer-support flow in CloverDX. A Normalizer expands eligible support-queue candidates for fan cases involving games, concerts, and live events. I want to standardize the event_title once and reuse it for every emitted queue candidate.

Input metadata (Port 0, name: FanSupportCasesIn):
- case_key: long
- event_title: string (nullable=false)
- queue_candidates: string (comma-separated queue names, nullable=true)
- case_is_open: boolean (nullable=false)

Output metadata (Port 0, name: FanSupportQueuesOut):
- case_key: long
- normalized_event_title: string
- support_queue: string
- queue_position: long

Can you show the Normalizer CTL2 code with count() and transform(idx)?

Only emit queue records when queue_candidates is not null and either case_is_open is true or event_title starts with `CANCELLED:`. When records are emitted, normalize event_title once by trimming it and converting it to uppercase, then reuse that normalized value for every queue candidate. Split queue_candidates on commas, trim each emitted support_queue value, and set queue_position from idx.

A candidate implementation to review:

```ctl
//#CTL2

string[] queues;
string normalizedTitle;

function integer count() {
    if (isnull($in.0.queue_candidates)
        && !(($in.0.case_is_open)
             || startsWith($in.0.event_title, "CANCELLED:"))) {
        return 0;
    }

    normalizedTitle = upperCase(trim($in.0.event_title));
    queues = split(nvl($in.0.queue_candidates, ""), ",");
    return length(queues);
}

function integer transform(integer idx) {
    $out.0.case_key = $in.0.case_key;
    $out.0.normalized_event_title = normalizedTitle;
    $out.0.support_queue = trim(queues[idx]);
    $out.0.queue_position = idx;
    return OK;
}

function void clean() {
    clear(queues);
    normalizedTitle = null;
}
```

Provide a corrected, complete answer. Briefly explain the essential fixes and why they are needed.

