Write the CTL2 transformation for a Reformat/Map component with input port 0 and output port 0.

Input metadata, port 0:
<Metadata id="BeneluxFreightLoyaltyIn">
  <Record name="BeneluxFreightLoyaltyIn_Record" type="delimited">
    <Field name="member_number" type="string" nullable="false"/>
    <Field name="haulage_scan_time" type="date" format="yyyy-MM-dd HH:mm:ss" nullable="false"/>
    <Field name="programme_market" type="string" nullable="false"/>
    <Field name="booked_product" type="string" nullable="false"/>
    <Field name="pallet_quantity" type="long" nullable="false"/>
    <Field name="chargeable_tonnes" type="decimal" nullable="false"/>
    <Field name="freight_charge_eur" type="decimal" nullable="false"/>
    <Field name="pickup_postcode" type="string"/>
    <Field name="dropoff_postcode" type="string"/>
    <Field name="consignment_reference" type="string" nullable="false"/>
    <Field name="cross_border_move" type="boolean"/>
  </Record>
</Metadata>

Lookup metadata: `BeneluxLoyaltySchemeLookup` is keyed by programme_market and returns programme_market (string), rewards_centre (string), regular_points_per_eur (decimal), priority_points_per_eur (decimal), and excluded_destination_prefixes (string list). The lookup has at most one row per key.

Output metadata, port 0:
<Metadata id="FreightRewardsPostingOut">
  <Record name="FreightRewardsPostingOut_Record" type="delimited">
    <Field name="member_number" type="string" nullable="false"/>
    <Field name="rewards_centre" type="string" nullable="false"/>
    <Field name="earning_category" type="string" nullable="false"/>
    <Field name="posting_day" type="date" format="yyyy-MM-dd" nullable="false"/>
    <Field name="credited_points" type="long" nullable="false"/>
    <Field name="route_result" type="string" nullable="false"/>
    <Field name="benefit_state" type="string" nullable="false"/>
    <Field name="exception_note" type="string"/>
  </Record>
</Metadata>

Business logic:
- Retrieve the loyalty-scheme lookup record using programme_market. If it is missing, set rewards_centre to UNCONFIGURED, earning_category to MANUAL, posting_day to the calendar-date portion of haulage_scan_time, credited_points to 0, route_result to MARKET_NOT_ENROLLED, benefit_state to ON_HOLD, and exception_note to MARKET_NOT_ENROLLED.
- Otherwise, route_result is ROUTE_DETAILS_MISSING when pickup_postcode or dropoff_postcode is null or empty. When both postcodes are present, route_result is EXCLUDED_DESTINATION if dropoff_postcode begins with any configured excluded-destination prefix; otherwise it is ACCEPTED.
- Set earning_category to PRIORITY when booked_product is PRIORITY or when cross_border_move is true and chargeable_tonnes is no more than 2. For all other accepted movements, use REGULAR. A movement with route_result other than ACCEPTED must have earning_category set to INELIGIBLE.
- posting_day is the calendar-date portion of haulage_scan_time. For an ACCEPTED route, credited_points is the whole-number result of freight_charge_eur multiplied by priority_points_per_eur for PRIORITY, or by regular_points_per_eur for REGULAR. Credited_points is 0 for INELIGIBLE.
- benefit_state is BONUS_REVIEW when an accepted movement is both cross-border and has a freight_charge_eur greater than 1000. It is QUALIFIED when route_result is ACCEPTED and bonus review does not apply. It is ON_HOLD for all other route results.
- exception_note is ROUTE_DETAILS_MISSING when route_result is ROUTE_DETAILS_MISSING, EXCLUDED_DESTINATION when route_result is EXCLUDED_DESTINATION, HIGH_VALUE_CROSS_BORDER when benefit_state is BONUS_REVIEW, and null otherwise. Apply these reasons in the stated precedence order. Emit one record.

Implementation clarifications:
- Use programme_market as the key to BeneluxLoyaltySchemeLookup. The posting day means the calendar-date portion of haulage_scan_time.
- Treat cross_border_move as false when it is null.
- For the EXCLUDED_DESTINATION test, compare dropoff_postcode against each string in the lookup field excluded_destination_prefixes; an absent or empty prefix list has no match. Route-result precedence is ROUTE_DETAILS_MISSING before EXCLUDED_DESTINATION before ACCEPTED.
- Only ACCEPTED routes may earn points. Convert the calculated decimal points amount to a long by retaining its whole-number portion.
- The priority earning rule is `(booked_product is PRIORITY) OR (cross_border_move is true AND chargeable_tonnes <= 2)`. Route eligibility overrides this result: a non-ACCEPTED route is always INELIGIBLE.

Lookup table definition:
- Lookup table ID: BeneluxLoyaltySchemeLookup.
- Lookup record metadata ID: BeneluxLoyaltySchemeLookupMeta.
