Incorrect assistant response to fix:
`transformOnError(string errorMessage, string stackTrace)` is invoked only after `transform()` fails. It receives the error text and stack trace, then can populate the output record and return `OK` to emit a recovered group-level invoice.

```ctl
//#CTL2
long expedienteCodigo;
integer feeCount;

function integer append() {
    expedienteCodigo = $in.0.expediente_codigo;
    feeCount++;
    return OK;
}

function integer transform() {
    if (feeCount == 0) {
        raiseError("No fee entries in group");
    }
    return SKIP;
}

function integer transformOnError(string errorMessage, string stackTrace) {
    $out.0.expediente_codigo = expedienteCodigo;
    $out.0.factura_resumen = isBlank(errorMessage) || contains(errorMessage, "IVA")
        ? "REVISAR IVA" : "INCIDENCIA DE FACTURACION";
    $out.0.alerta_proceso = errorMessage;
    return OK;
